// Unreal-side entry file for the voxel-core GPU kernels (ADR-0006, G2a).
//
// This file deliberately contains NO logic. It exists because Unreal compiles
// a shader by (virtual file path, entry point name), and because the kernels
// themselves live outside the Unreal project — in voxel-core/shaders, which is
// engine-free and shared with the standalone Vulkan determinism bench.
//
// Keeping the kernels there rather than copying them here is the whole point:
// the M0/G1 gate proves the GPU output is bit-exact with the CPU mesher, and
// that proof only transfers to Unreal if Unreal compiles THE SAME TEXT. A copy
// would drift, silently, and the first symptom would be wrong terrain.
//
// Platform.ush must come first — it defines the per-platform intrinsics and
// type plumbing every Unreal shader is compiled against.
//
// VXC_UE is defined by FVoxelWorldGenShader::ModifyCompilationEnvironment. It
// switches worldgen.ush's resource DECLARATIONS (not its math) over to
// Unreal's conventions: no explicit register() slots, and the WorldGenParams
// fields declared as loose globals so they land in $Globals where Unreal's
// shader parameter struct binds them.

#include "/Engine/Public/Platform.ush"
#include "/VoxelCore/worldgen.ush"
